{
  "sn35.232:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.232 ",
  "sn35.232:0.2": "18. The Ocean ",
  "sn35.232:0.3": "With Koṭṭhita ",
  "sn35.232:1.1": "At one time Venerable Sāriputta and Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita were staying near Varanasi in the deer park at Isipatana. ",
  "sn35.232:1.2": "Then in the late afternoon, Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita came out of retreat, went to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn35.232:1.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "sn35.232:2.1": "“Reverend Sāriputta, which is it? Is the eye the fetter of sights, or are sights the fetter of the eye? ",
  "sn35.232:2.2": "Is the ear … nose … tongue … body … ",
  "sn35.232:2.3": "mind the fetter of ideas, or are ideas the fetter of the mind?” ",
  "sn35.232:3.1": "“Reverend Koṭṭhita, the eye is not the fetter of sights, nor are sights the fetter of the eye. ",
  "sn35.232:3.2": "The fetter there is the desire and greed that arises from the pair of them. ",
  "sn35.232:3.3": "The ear … nose … tongue … body … ",
  "sn35.232:3.4": "",
  "sn35.232:3.5": "mind is not the fetter of ideas, nor are ideas the fetter of the mind. ",
  "sn35.232:3.6": "The fetter there is the desire and greed that arises from the pair of them. ",
  "sn35.232:4.1": "Suppose there was a black ox and a white ox yoked by a single harness or yoke. ",
  "sn35.232:4.2": "Would it be right to say that ",
  "sn35.232:4.3": "the black ox is the yoke of